// Proofs for the identities barista.hana states, in the strategy language of
// docs/proving.md. An identity with no entry here is proved by `diagram`
// alone — this file holds exactly the claims that need direction.

// The contract claim, and the corpus's biggest goal: 351 boxes against 2
// once `inline` has opened it. It closes as a decision tree of three
// hypotheses, and the tree is the splits' own: a `cases` is η on its wire
// and then the branch that makes split by `select-same`, so each case is
// an independent goal written inside it.
//
// Each split names its wire by address — as much of the box's name as the
// listing emphasised, read off the goal as the step before it leaves it.
//
// One state decides everything: `emit` dispatches on `equal(x.2,
// state::thirsty)`, which is `#uk`, and the driver has already identified
// that test with the precondition disjunction's own — one wire, two
// readers. Its false case closes outright: `emit` answers a false flag, so
// the postcondition holds whatever the precondition said and the whole
// disjunction is moot. Its true case resolves `emit`; the tuple rows
// (`tuple-cancel`, `as-tuple-built`, `equal-refl`) take the
// postcondition's shape guards apart until its symbol checks are the very
// boxes the precondition tested, and the two `is_symbol` splits — `#lq` on
// the payload's second field, then `#oz` on its first — decide them. Each
// false case is discharged by `and-literal` and each true case folds the
// conjunction shut, which is why every leaf here is a bare `diagram`.
//
// `#oz`'s readers are created inside `#lq`'s true case, which is why that
// split sits there rather than beside it.
proof barista::customer_impl::emit_does_pre_and_post_is_constant =
    inline both(decide)
    cases(#uk) (
        true: both(decide) cases(#lq) (
            true: both(decide) cases(#oz) (true: diagram, false: diagram),
            false: diagram),
        false: diagram);
